            <ArticleTitle>Macular hole in Stargardt disease: Clinical and ultra-structural observation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>486-489</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/13816810.2016.1266666</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="PURPOSE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To report for the first time a case report of a Stargardt disease patient who developed a macular hole (MH) which was treated with a surgical approach.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHOD" NlmCategory="METHODS">Case report.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">After vitrectomy a complete closure of the MH was obtained and the best-corrected visual acuity remained stable. No complications were reported after one year of follow-up. An ultra-structural examination of the removed internal limiting membrane (ILM) and epiretinal membrane (ERM) was carried out under electron microscopy.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Vitreo-retinal surgery could represent a therapeutic option to treat vitreo-retinal interface abnormalities associated with inherited retinal diseases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
